# Price grid, Professional rows (TC-296 – TC-313): from Standard 08:00, trim to 00:30, tap Professional (no toast),
# then the fps and Resolution chips, and read the CTA price and 「Selected Length」 at 00:30, 01:30, the 02:30 cap and
# 00:30 again; ends by tapping Standard and pushing the selection back to 08:00 for the next row.
# Charges nothing: Enhance is never tapped.
# Starts and ends: as price-grid-standard.steps (ve-1230-1080p30 panel scrolled down, Standard, 00:00–08:00, the style
# already set: tap chip_style_natural / chip_style_sharp before the block, no cap bubble).
# Args: $1 = case ID, $2 = fps chip id, $3 = resolution chip id.
# Coordinates (SM-A5360, 16.9.0 2611091, measured 2026-11-18): Professional keeps the Standard strip scale (~0.587 s
# per pixel), so finger 212 = 「00:30」 (30.x s), 315 = 「01:30」 (90.x s), 1060 pushes to the 02:30 cap, where the
# handle is grabbed at x 416. Wait 3 s after a cap push (the cap bubble swallows the next touch).
case $1
fingerdrag 980 1158 212 1158 20
fingerdrag 540 1750 540 1250 10
id chip_mode_professional
expect-not "supports clips|Shorten your selection"
id $2
id $3
wait 1
els chip_
els tv_
shot $1-chips
fingerdrag 540 1250 540 1750 10
wait 1
els tv_
shot $1-30s
fingerdrag 212 1158 315 1158 20
els tv_
shot $1-90s
fingerdrag 315 1158 1060 1158 15
shot $1-cap
wait 3
els tv_
fingerdrag 416 1158 212 1158 20
els tv_
els chip_
shot $1-back30
id chip_mode_standard
fingerdrag 212 1158 1060 1158 15
wait 3
